<title>BELGIUM: Chemical container fall blocks Belgo-Dutch canal.</title>
<headline>Chemical container fall blocks Belgo-Dutch canal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twenty-eight containers which could be holding harmful chemicals fell from a ship in a canal north of the Belgian port of Antwerp, canal authorities said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;For the moment the canal is closed,&quot; Adrian Vermin from a canal administration body told Reuters by telephone, adding that the waterway was the main inland route for ships between Antwerp and Rotterdam in the Netherlands.</p>
<p>Vermin said the containers fell from the ship on a stretch of the canal near the Dutch border at about 1030 GMT on Monday night.</p>
